{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfe2Y453djCW6cvkmoAaU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted the portfolio, and its validation Sharpe is **−0.60**, against **0.45** in training, so it failed out of sample. It holds the 126-day time-series momentum signals long and the 5-day momentum, 21-day momentum and 21/63 moving-average signals in reverse (betting on short-term reversal), equal-weighted across all 47 industries and scaled to equal risk per group.\n\nI built it using only the 1970–1999 training data and called the backtest service once before submitting. The training data was already discouraging. On average the individual signals had negative Sharpe ratios. When I split training into two halves, how the signals ranked in the first half was negatively related to how they ranked in the second (rank correlation −0.19). So simply picking the best signals in-sample doesn't carry over. The four groups I chose were the only ones that were profitable, in the direction I traded them, in both halves.\n\nI didn't use the 5000 backtest calls to search for a portfolio with a better validation number. With 423 signals this weak, a portfolio chosen that way would have a high validation Sharpe mostly by luck. That figure would no longer be a fair out-of-sample test."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":9629,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8c9cbee-97a3-46d6-8046-124aa9101a38","uuid":"185f8190-e83d-42ca-b2fb-9b82abade077","timestamp":"2026-10-02T20:17:38.441Z","request_id":"req_011Cfe2Y3pAkuxQtF6pBZTMK"}
